    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0789" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Stam, John C./67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-19T19:00:00+08:00">February 19, 1935—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 19—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. Reference Legation’s 81, February 18, 8 p.m., following telegram has been
                    received from Peck at Nanking: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 19, 2 p.m. My February 18, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="84"
                                xml:id="d662-f1"/> last paragraph. <pb facs="0790" n="678"
                                xml:id="pg678"/> I delivered message to Director Liu February 19, 11
                            a.m. and he said the Foreign Office stated [it] would release the
                            information.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
